  "articleBody": "Putting up fresh drywall seems straightforward until you face out-of-square rooms or heavy ceiling panels. Here is how to know when to bring in an experienced installer.\n\n- Framing is out of plane: If your studs or joists are uneven, a pro knows how to shim and prep surfaces so finished walls look flat.\n- Tall or complex ceilings: Lifting, holding, and fastening heavy panels overhead requires specialized lifts and hands-on skill.\n- High-visibility or critical lighting: Rooms with large windows or raking light reveal every slight hump. Getting a smooth, seamless finish requires expert taping.\n- Fire-rated assemblies involved: Garages and utility rooms often require specialized fire-rated boards with strict fastener spacing and inspection needs.\n- Layouts with lots of corners and cuts: Complex floor plans with soffits, niches, and arches demand precise cuts to prevent wasted materials.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nAn experienced contractor checks behind-the-wall work, chooses the right panel thickness, and coordinates the schedule so mudding and painting go smoothly. \n\nPlanning a remodel or fresh drywall installation? Call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your project scope today.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
